{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779084099,"nonce":"S4c6CRCSOMbGo4Sr60UfVJIr7fQ=","title":"Phase 4d: complete Studio train-eval-analysis-report vertical path","message":"## Parent / coordination\n- Roadmap: `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap, Phase 4.\n- Studio pipeline spec: `0c46f69`.\n- Structural authoring spec: `5378a5d`.\n- Bottom-pane collection issue: `4e0d925`.\n- Prior Phase 4 slices: `b424865`, `ddd3758`, `ff19bc8`.\n- Real training backend dependency/context: `e57ae1f`.\n\n## Problem\nThe merged Studio pipeline MVP gives Studio a durable workspace, active train-stage scenario ownership, provider execution-plan preparation, and a local execution path that materializes spec snapshots and attaches refs. Phase 4 is still not complete because the Studio product path stops at the train-stage run. Eval, analysis, and report stages do not yet consume upstream stage collections through the workspace model, and the local execution path still behaves like a validation/materialization runner rather than a usable product vertical slice.\n\n## Scope\nFinish the first ugly-but-real Phase 4 vertical path without narrowing Phase 5 or later product work:\n\n- Preserve the existing `StudioWorkspaceSpec` / provider `ExecutionSpec` boundary.\n- Add the missing train -\u003e eval -\u003e analysis -\u003e report stage flow over durable workspace collections.\n- Make eval stages consume the train-stage output collection and carry explicit inherited/forkable scenario references.\n- Make analysis stages consume eval/artifact collections and emit manifest/artifact refs through the workspace model.\n- Add a minimal report/product stub stage over analysis outputs, with manifest/artifact refs rather than hidden UI state.\n- Replace or augment the current local validation/materialization execution with a real MVP training-result artifact where feasible, while keeping full JAX worker replacement tracked by `e57ae1f` if broader graph compilation remains out of scope.\n- Wire backend APIs plus frontend store/UI actions enough for the user to progress through the vertical path from Studio.\n- Add tests for stage collection propagation, manifest/artifact refs, and save/load preservation.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No full Phase 5 ownership refactor across all existing Studio state.\n- No polished bottom-pane timeline/graph UX.\n- No live SSH/RunPod/Modal submission.\n- No Mandible UI work in this Feedbax branch.\n- No irreversible schema narrowing that blocks richer eval protocols, analysis DAGs, reports, visual objective authoring, or cloud execution later.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- From a saved/restored Studio workspace, a user can run or materialize the train stage, then materialize eval, analysis, and report stages that consume upstream collections.\n- Each stage records status, input/output collection refs, manifest refs, artifact refs, and executed snapshot refs where relevant.\n- Eval scenarios explicitly inherit from or fork the training scenario.\n- Analysis and report stages are represented as typed workspace stages, not only frontend-only page state.\n- Backend and frontend tests cover the vertical path and preserve future/custom stage metadata.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}